WEBVTT

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.210
The mystery meat
lunch set?

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.700
Can't you eat
a lunch with some class?

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.200
Leave me alone.
This food is the most filling.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.170
Break a chopstick,
and you'll cause a disaster.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.070
Grandma always
says so!

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.190
That's just superstition.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.230
I'd be careful
if I were you.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.760
Grandma is never wrong!

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.500
That jerk, Sakamoto.
He always says the dumbest things.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.360
You okay down there?

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.760
Oh, Godai.
It's only you.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.860
It just slipped out of my hands.
Sorry 'bout that.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.040
''Sorry.''
Yeah, sure she is.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:23.830
Geez.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.070
A hundred yen!

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.380
It's mine!

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.390
Break a chopstick,
and you'll cause a disaster.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.510
Grandma always
says so.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.340
I-It couldn't be!

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.040
That's the spirit!

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.590
Ms. Otonashi!

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.850
Are you okay,
Ms. Otonashi!?

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.670
I-I'm fine--

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:04.970
Oww!

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:07.860
Let me have a look.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:11.760
Does this hurt?

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:12.850
Yeah, a little.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.120
It's a sprain.
Forgive me.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.580
That volley was
too advanced.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:16.650
Not at all. I'm just
not skilled enough--
That volley was
too advanced.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.360
Not at all. I'm just
not skilled enough--

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:21.950
It's my fault.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.760
Oh, it really isn't that serious--

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.720
I'll take you
to the hospital.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.870
P-Please put me down.
You're overreacting.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:37.640
No!

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.870
Ain't you the bold one?

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.240
Sweepin' her away
in front of everybody.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.320
Don't make weird assumptions.
It's a coach's duty.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.550
Then if I got hurt,
you'd carry me, too?

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.630
Don't strain
yourself to answer.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:11.180
I'm so sorry to make you go
to all this work for me.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.290
A friend in need--

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.720
Just get better, okay?

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:17.940
Thank you.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.980
Ms. Otonashi?
Have you finished dressing?

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:22.480
Yes! Come in.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.500
Still out of bed?
Let me help you back in--

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.320
No, I'm fine. I'm really--

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.850
Don't overexerrt yourself.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:35.290
Why's he goin'
the long way 'round?

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.420
Ask him for yourself.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:40.920
Really?
I didn't realize.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.430
Careful not to slide
into bed with her.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:53.860
H-How you jest.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.530
What'd happen if
he slid into bed?

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.860
Ask him for yourself.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.790
M-Mrs. Ichinose, you cad.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.930
Manager, you're hurt?

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:04.310
It's nothing.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.400
How'd it happen?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.360
It happened while
we were playing tennis.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.020
Well, you're makin' up for it;
helpin' out.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.480
Because it's my fault.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.710
Why don't you
sleep here tonight?

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.810
Excuse me. I'm
talking to Ms. Otonashi.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.360
Ms. Otonashi, until
you're completely healed--

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.340
Why don't you
sleep here tonight?

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.510
Ms. Otonashi, I'll take
full responsibility--

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.210
Come up and play.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.690
Responsibility for
your grievous--

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.240
Come, now--

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:34.790
Take care of me!

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:35.870
And me, as well.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:36.690
Me, too!

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:38.800
Keep it down.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.880
Don't mind them.
Just lie back.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:41.720
Okay.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.330
You're hurt. You gotta
have peace and quiet.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.390
Thank you.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.740
Never mind the background noise,
just get some sleep.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:49.860
I will.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:52.930
Let's party!

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:02.960
That's Mitaka's car!

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.630
What is that jerk
doing here so late?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.010
What's wrong?
You're not looking good.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.490
Do you have
a stomach ache?

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:19.760
This party's swinging!

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.560
Manager, have one on me.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.460
Thanks. But I--

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.830
Come in--

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.700
Welcome home.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.080
M-Manager!

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.940
Wh-What's wrong!?
Are you sick!?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.310
No, no! I only--

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:39.600
Voila.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:40.630
Mr. Yotsuya!

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:42.090
What are you doing?

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.790
Y-Your leg!

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.540
It's my fault!

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.330
I'm so sorry.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:59.670
If only I hadn't broken
that chopstick at lunch--

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.030
But, my sprain...

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:04.730
...is my fault.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.720
My volley was impossible to return.
She hurt her leg trying.

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.480
No, I just wasn't
careful enough--

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.620
No! It's my fault!

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.980
No, I said
it's my fault!

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.190
E-Excuse me.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:23.840
Who cares whose
fault it is?

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.540
Time to break up this
cheer-up-the-manager party.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.890
Goodness
look at the time.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.410
Kyoko, get well soon.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.140
Thank you.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:39.860
Umm--

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.590
Manager, I--

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.880
What'cha doing?
The party's over.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.550
Let go. I need to
talk to the manager!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.400
We'll relay anything
you want to say.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.530
But-- Manager!

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:05.750
Believe me. Her ankle
is all my fault!

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.840
You're not
makin' any sense.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.220
And since I'm
the reason she--

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.010
What am I gonna do!?

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.120
I know!
I'll nurse her back to health!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.520
No way we're letting you traipse
around in the manager's room!

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.130
Don't get any ideas.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.390
You're wrong!
Let go!

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:28.540
Yotsuya!

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.230
Where are you
going with that pillow?

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.140
To apply some TLC--

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:35.630
C'mon, kid!
Chug it down.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:37.430
But I'm--

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.790
It don't matter.
Drink up!

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.430
Manag--

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:42.930
Ma--

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.380
I'm off!
Bye, Soichiro.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:03.930
I still can't
stand on it.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:07.990
Yes?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.960
Manager?
You awake?

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.810
Y-Yes--
Come in.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:14.890
Good morning.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:18.490
Good morning.
You're up early.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.200
Yeah... You know.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.380
You're looking pale.
Didn't you sleep last night?

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.560
I was so
worried about you--

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.850
If there's
anything I can do--

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.320
Oh, no. I'm fine!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:38.110
But your injury was
all because of me.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.450
But--

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:41.780
It's all my fault!

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.310
Please allow me
to care for you!

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.680
But don't you
have classes?

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.880
I'll cut 'em!
It's just school!

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.200
Don't say that!
Show more commitment!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:55.720
I'm committed to YOU!

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:00.790
What'cha doing? Bothering a lady
while she's in bed--

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.450
Godai was
worried about me.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:07.400
I guess you don't have courage
enough to slide into bed with her.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:09.660
W-What does
that mean?

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.280
Here's what we
had to spare.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.420
Thank you.

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:14.120
You really don't have
much to spare.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.470
She'll never get
better on that.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.710
Just get yourself
off to school.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.050
B-But--

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.550
Leave the
manager to me.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.630
She's not going to get better
any faster with you here.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:29.340
B-But--

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.310
Yo! Godai!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:44.030
Let's get some lunch!

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:45.120
I'll pass!

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.650
What's he in
such a hurry for?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.540
Hello? Is this
Maison Ikkoku?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:57.600
Affirmative.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.820
Oh, Yotsuya. How is
the manager feeling?

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.300
She is curt, but Fine.
Goodbye--

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:08.010
Wait a second.
What about lunch?

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.360
Licked the plate clean.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:12.100
What'd they Fix?

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:16.950
2 rice balls: bonito and pickled plum,
and 3 pickled radish slices.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.350
That's all?

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.170
You don't approve?

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.400
I-It's okay.
Thanks.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.800
Leftovers for breakfast
and 2 rice balls for lunch!--

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.380
I gotta do something.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:37.260
Okay.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:05.100
The basis of ''white stew''
is its light seasonings.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:09.350
The secret is to avoid pan frying in oil;
instead, douse with wine.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:12.030
And simmer thoroughly
over a low flame.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.220
You're an expert!

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.750
Good.
Cooking is an art!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.970
It requires sensitivity
and great creativity.

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:30.080
I never knew you were
such a talented cook.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:34.250
Then you've begun to
understand the kind of man I am.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.340
It's done.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:44.630
It looks delicious!

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.970
Then please try some.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:48.140
I will!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.360
Be my guest.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.470
How is it?

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.560
It's wonderful!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.050
It's so good.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.550
You're an excellent cook!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:03.540
I enjoy it.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.370
I suppose it
isn't very masculine.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.650
Oh, no! That's
not true at all!

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.290
But, all this trouble--

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.430
Don't let it bother you.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:16.960
Just to be of some service
makes me the happiest of men.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:23.000
Every word outta his mouth
is over dramatic hogwash.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:27.200
--His parents are at fault.
--Who cares? He's gorgeous!

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.810
Maybe I'll sprain
my ankle, too.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:32.190
Go ahead.
You'll starve to death.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.100
189.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.140
51.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.130
238.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.480
36.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.710
That'll be 623 yen.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:53.860
That much!?

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.710
623 yen please.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.050
I'm 18 short.

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:02.610
--Can--?
--623 yen please.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:04.260
Okay.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.160
Put this back.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.010
Geez!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.550
I can't do anything classy
for her on my budget.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.300
If only I could
buy her roses...

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.510
They're beautiful.
Godai, thank you!

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.350
They're such a comfort!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.790
Then I'm glad I went
into debt for them.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.640
Is that how
much you love me?

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.170
Manager!

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.580
''Add two cups of
water to the soup base--''

00:14:58.860 --> 00:14:59.760
Water!
Water!

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:04.580
That was close--

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.300
I can't breathe.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.000
But Coach Mitaka's cooking was
so good I had to eat everything.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.760
Manager, how ya feelin'?

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:18.610
Fine.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:20.810
Guess what?

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:24.590
It'll cheer you up.
Dig in.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.240
It is but a trifle
yet from the heart.

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.750
Please, while
they're hot--

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.840
They're terrible
when they're cold.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:34.310
Okay--

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.670
I, uh--

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.400
--They're good...
--...aren't they?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:49.760
They're great!
But there's so much--

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:53.600
You mustn't hold back.
Eat it all.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.910
We bought it
just for you!

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.390
O-Oh, I'll eat it, all right.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:18.140
M-Manager,
it's ready!

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.980
That does it. I've eaten
more than I can take.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:26.820
I feel awful.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.030
Manager?
Can I come in?

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.190
Godai?
Come in.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.770
I-It couldn't be--

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:44.820
I-I thought that you might be hungry.
It's the best I can do.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:46.840
I--

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.420
I can't refuse
a face like that.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:54.680
Of course
I'll have some.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.450
My, what a pretty cosmos flower--

00:16:57.980 --> 00:17:00.790
It was blooming in the
garden. Instead of roses.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:03.170
It's getting cold.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.800
I just love a
cosmos in bloom.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:06.930
And soggy.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.300
O-Oh, yeah.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:11.360
H-Here I go.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:28.670
Is it good?

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:31.260
Y-Yes, very!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.810
S-She ate everything!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.660
Manager!

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:05.340
S-She ate an entire
bowl of awful ramen!

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:08.510
What a sweet woman!

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:31.240
Sweet buns AND
fried octopus?

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.720
Yup, and she
put it all away!

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.570
You fed her ramen?

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.830
And Coach Mitaka cooked
for her, before that.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:41.380
She could've
said something.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:48.140
On top of all of that, she ate
a mountain of my rotten ramen.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.020
And she smiled at me.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.650
The mark of
true greatness.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.160
Oh, no!

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:02.790
Enough of this. I'm sick of
being treated like a sick person.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.230
Manager!

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:11.240
--I'm coming in--
--Wait!

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.750
You--You creep!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:25.690
What's going on!?

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.870
--What's the commotion?
--It's nothing!

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:31.530
Hey! Manager!
You okay!?

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.140
It's nothing!

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.480
What happened--?

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:38.250
Don't look!

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:40.070
Whazza matter?

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.590
It was really nothing.

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:49.250
Takin' advantage of an invalid!
You oughta be ashamed--

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:50.420
It's a
misunderstanding!

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:53.130
I'd say we're
understandin' it perfectly!

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:54.780
You're wrong!

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.310
You should slap him upside
the head 2 or 3 times.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:02.180
I was taking a
sponge bath, and--

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.630
Well, that's dull.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.600
I said it
was a mistake.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:07.980
I wonder...

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.770
I'm sorry
I didn't wait--

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:13.420
Whatever; just
close the door!

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:14.710
I'm so sorry!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.080
Honestly!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.460
''Upset stomach''?
So that's it.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:36.130
Huh? The coach
is here again?

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:37.870
I'm home, Soichiro!

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:41.180
Here! Some leftover
bread from lunch.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.060
You'll eat
anythin', won'tcha?

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:47.390
What? You overate!?

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.780
My stomach--

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:54.530
What a shame. I was going to fix
my specialty: shrimp au gratin.

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:56.010
I'm sorry.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:57.710
Yes?

00:20:58.550 --> 00:20:59.570
Sorry about
this morning--

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:07.340
Roses!

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.440
What made that
bump on your head?

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:17.870
It's nothing.

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.180
ls that from
the wash-pail?

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.670
A little bump like
this is nothing.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.710
I'm sorry. And I threw
it as hard as I could.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.800
It's okay.
I had it coming.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:28.920
But--

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:28.950
I told you
not to worry.
But--

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:30.470
I told you
not to worry.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:32.240
Then you're okay?

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:33.850
I'm just fine.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:36.790
Mind if I cook? It'd be
a shame to waste food.

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:38.600
But--

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:40.040
Try it, Godai.

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.090
You don't know how good
Coach Mitaka's cooking is.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:45.710
I-- I see.

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:48.900
So, Godai, what
happened to your head?

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:54.960
I can't say. It's a secret
between the manager and me.

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:56.510
Honestly, Godai--

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:06.670
Godai, would you
mind opening a can?

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:07.960
Sure, my pleasure.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:11.600
So, what happened!?

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:13.550
It's open.

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:17.730
--Well!?
--It's a secret.

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.230
I was asking you to
set out the plates.

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:26.100
Well, why didn't
you say so?

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:28.040
Plates, plates...

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:32.000
Well, here it is.

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:35.410
Be my guest.

00:22:35.650 --> 00:22:36.550
Thank you.

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:38.010
Yeah, thanks.

00:22:38.650 --> 00:22:40.170
It won't be
anything spec--

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:44.450
How is it?

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:47.290
--Good.
--Huh? What's that?

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:48.960
It's very good.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.730
Think so?
That's great!

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:53.000
It really is delicious.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:59.180
Whoever marries you is going
to be one happy woman.

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:05.200
You know, I was just
thinking that very thing!

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:09.140
If someone would marry me,
she'd be one happy woman!

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:10.650
But I--

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:12.520
Don't you think so, Godai?

00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:13.980
W-Who knows?

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:21.600
I was just speaking
hypothetically!

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:23.400
Just hypothetically--

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:25.140
I--

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:28.340
The two of you--
couldn't be--

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:30.240
Honestly!

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:52.820
They say that happiness is
marrying your first love.

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:57.360
You can live your whole life with
that person, and never be parted.

00:23:58.230 --> 00:24:01.920
Next: ''The Story of Kyoko's First Love.
On Rainy Days Like These...''

00:24:02.570 --> 00:24:05.730
Soichiro isn't around to invite me
under his umbrella, anymore.
